## Schema Design

User

- id (Primary Key)  
- email (Unique)  
- created_at  

VideoAsset

- id (Primary Key)  
- user_id (Foreign Key → User.id)  
- storage_url  
- status (uploaded / processing / ready)  
- created_at  

Job

- id (Primary Key)  
- video_id (Foreign Key → VideoAsset.id)  
- type (transcription / summary / highlights)  
- status (queued / processing / success / failed)  
- retry_count  
- created_at  

JobEvent

- id (Primary Key)  
- job_id (Foreign Key → Job.id)  
- event_type  
- timestamp  
- metadata (JSON)  

Artifact

- id (Primary Key)  
- job_id (Foreign Key → Job.id)  
- type (transcript / summary / screenshot)  
- storage_url  
- created_at  

Highlight

- id (Primary Key)  
- video_id (Foreign Key → VideoAsset.id)  
- start_time  
- end_time  
- label  

---

## Key Constraints / Indexes

Constraints

- UNIQUE(User.email)  
- FK(VideoAsset.user_id → User.id)  
- FK(Job.video_id → VideoAsset.id)  
- FK(Artifact.job_id → Job.id)  

Indexes

- Index on Job.video_id  
- Index on Job.status  
- Index on Artifact.job_id  
- Index on Highlight.video_id  

These indexes optimize frequent lookup and job tracking operations.

---

## Job Lifecycle

Jobs follow a simple state machine:

queued → processing → success / failed

Workers are designed to be idempotent, allowing safe retries without generating duplicate artifacts. Retries are controlled using retry_count with a capped limit.

---

## Storage Layout

Artifacts are stored in object storage using structured paths:

/videos/{video_id}/original.mp4  
/videos/{video_id}/transcript.json  
/videos/{video_id}/summary.md  
/videos/{video_id}/highlights.json  
/videos/{video_id}/screenshots/

Safe Download Strategy

Files are never publicly exposed. The API Service generates pre-signed URLs after validating user authorization. This prevents unauthorized access and reduces backend bandwidth usage.

